/**
@mainpage Arches HAL Reference

@section overview Overview

Arches HAL is the C++17 hardware abstraction and validation layer for the
Jetson (Tegra, L4T/JetPack) plus its STM32 real-time co-processor. It is
two things at once:

- A hardware test-suite framework: one binary per module, all sharing the
  same `TestBase` / `runTestApp<T>()` CLI (one-shot, monitoring,
  long-term, monitor-test, event).
- The canonical proto/gRPC contract source for the fleet. Arches-Client
  and Arches-Server link this repo and never regenerate its generated
  symbols.

@section layout Layout

- `src/<module>_lib/` — one library per hardware module, each a `TestBase`
  subclass, paired with `tests/<module>/` and `protos/modules/<id>.proto`.
- `src/lib_base.h` / `.cpp` — the shared `TestBase`, `TestOutput`,
  `hal::Status`, `hal::Value` framework every module subclasses.
- `src/test_runner.h` — `runTestApp<T>()`, the template that gives every
  module binary its uniform CLI.
- `src/platform_arches.h` — Jetson platform constants (SoC family,
  L4T/JetPack OS, CPU core range, thermal limits, GPU render node,
  devfreq/thermal-zone paths) plus the STM32 UART/SPI framing constants.
- `src/stm32_transport.h` / `.cpp` + `src/mcu_interface_lib/` — the STM32
  co-processor link (`Stm32Transport`): GPIO/SPI/UART/DMS pass-through,
  secondary-MCU redundancy, failover, sync.
- `protos/hal_service.proto` — the stable gRPC contract; module
  config/result are `google.protobuf.Any`, so adding a module never
  changes an RPC signature.
- `protos/client_service.proto` — the bidi streaming contract, package
  `arches.stream`.
- `protos/registry/modules.yaml` — the machine-readable module manifest
  every consumer reads.

@section modules The modules

audio_interfaces, camera_interfaces, camera_module3, clock_and_timing,
communication_interface, cpu, debug_and_development_interfaces,
deep_learning_accelerator, display_interfaces, environmental, ethernet,
ethernet_switch, external_connector, functional_safety, gnss, gpio, gpu,
imu, mcu_interface, pcie, poe_hat, power_management, reliability,
security_features, sense_hat, serializer_deserializer, software_interface,
storage, system_integration, system_memory, thermal_management, usb,
video_encode_decode, vision_accelerator, watchdog_and_reset.

49 proto contracts exist against 35 implemented modules by design — the
extra 14 are reserved for hardware coverage that hasn't landed in `src/`
yet. Browse `protos/registry/modules.yaml` in the source listing below for
the full manifest.

@section building Building this documentation

```
make doc          # HTML (+ XML, man) via Doxygen — needs doxygen, graphviz
make doc-pdf       # also builds docs/Arches-HAL-Reference.pdf — needs pdflatex
make install-tools # installs doxygen/graphviz/texlive if missing
```

Output lands under `build/native/docs/` (`html/`, `latex/`,
`Arches-HAL-Reference.pdf`, `xml/`, `man/`). Nothing under `build/` is
version-controlled.

@note Coverage of `\brief`/`\param` style comments across the 35 modules
is a work in progress — `WARN_LOGFILE` in the Doxygen run lists what's
still undocumented without failing the build (see `Doxyfile.in`).
*/
